msgid "SMTP Relay: test connection"
msgstr ""

msgid "The form has expired. Open the page again and retry."
msgstr ""

msgid "The recipient is not a valid e-mail address."
msgstr ""

msgid "Off - nothing is routed, the relay is not even hooked in"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shadow - decide and log what would go via the relay, but send everything the normal way"
msgstr ""

msgid "On - matching mailings are sent via the relay"
msgstr ""

msgid "Mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "Start with Shadow during a real mailing and check the log (channel smtprelay) before switching to On. Test the relay without sending anything at civicrm/admin/setting/smtprelay/test."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rule: CiviMail mailings with at least this many recipients"
msgstr ""

msgid "A non-test CiviMail mailing with at least this many recipients goes via the relay. 0 switches this rule off. Test mailings, scheduled reminders, CiviRules and other single mails never match: only CiviMail bulk mail (VERP header X-CiviMail-Bounce plus Precedence: bulk) can be routed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rule: always these mailing IDs"
msgstr ""

msgid "Comma-separated CiviMail mailing IDs that always go via the relay, whatever their size (for example a single large campaign). Leave empty to use only the size rule."
msgstr ""

msgid "Relay host"
msgstr ""

msgid "For example smtp-relay.gmail.com (Google Workspace SMTP relay service) or the SMTP host of a bulk provider. The host must resolve to public addresses only. Empty = relay not configured: matching mailings wait (or fall back, see On failure)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Relay port"
msgstr ""

msgid "Allowed: 25, 465, 587 or 2525."
msgstr ""

msgid "STARTTLS (usually port 587)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Implicit TLS (usually port 465)"
msgstr ""

msgid "None (local testing only, never with authentication)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Encryption"
msgstr ""

msgid "EHLO name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Name sent in EHLO. Empty = the domain of the sender address. Google rejects \"localhost\"."
msgstr ""

msgid "None - the relay trusts the server IP address"
msgstr ""

msgid "Username and password"
msgstr ""

msgid "OAuth token of oauth_outgoing_mail (XOAUTH2)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

msgid "OAuth reuses the system token that the OAuth Outgoing Mail extension keeps for the sender address; no password is stored. The token only goes to the relay of its own provider (Google: smtp-relay.gmail.com or smtp.gmail.com, port 587 with STARTTLS or 465 with implicit TLS); other hosts are refused. Choosing or changing OAuth requires the permission \"manage OAuth client secrets\". Credentials are only ever sent over TLS."
msgstr ""

msgid "Username"
msgstr ""

msgid "Only for Authentication = Username and password. With OAuth the username comes from the token (the mailbox address)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Password"
msgstr ""

msgid "Only for Authentication = Username and password. Stored encrypted with CiviCRM crypto (key tag CRED; without CIVICRM_CRED_KEYS the value stays readable in the database) and never shown again. Leave empty to keep the stored password; after changing host, port or username enter it again."
msgstr ""

msgid "Envelope sender (bounces)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Rewrites the envelope sender (Return-Path) of relayed mail. Empty = keep the CiviMail VERP address. Set it to a monitored mailbox (for example the one your bounce processing reads) if the VERP addresses of your domain have no mailbox. The X-CiviMail-Bounce header stays, so CiviCRM still recognises the bounce."
msgstr ""

msgid "Refuse - pause the mailing; CiviMail resumes it in a later run"
msgstr ""

msgid "Fall back - send that message via the normal route"
msgstr ""

msgid "On failure of the relay"
msgstr ""

msgid "Refuse is safest when the reason for the relay is a daily quota on the normal route: falling back would use up exactly that quota. Either way a relay problem never counts as a bounce, and a message the relay may already have accepted (an error during DATA) is not sent again via the normal route."
msgstr ""

msgid "SMTP Relay settings"
msgstr ""

msgid "The relay host, port or username changed: enter the password again."
msgstr ""

msgid "Credentials are only sent over TLS: choose STARTTLS or implicit TLS, or set Authentication to None."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choosing OAuth or changing its relay host, port or encryption requires the permission \"manage OAuth client secrets\"."
msgstr ""

msgid "With OAuth the relay host must belong to the token provider (Google: smtp-relay.gmail.com or smtp.gmail.com, port 587 with STARTTLS or 465 with implicit TLS)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Handshake with the relay: connect, authenticate, MAIL FROM and RCPT TO, then RSET. No message is sent (DATA is never issued)."
msgstr ""

